WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.245
Think of a brand you can buy in almost any country, such as a big fast-food chain or a phone maker. A business that produces or sells in more than one country is called a multinational.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:25.088
Globalisation is the growth of trade and business links across the whole world. It brings opportunities, like selling to customers abroad online, and threats, like more foreign competition.

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:32.178
Keep the two terms apart. Globalisation is a worldwide trend. A multinational is one business.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:43.049
Step one: decide whose side the question takes. Is it the business itself, or the host country, where the multinational locates? The benefits are different.

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:53.179
The host country can also lose out. Profits may be sent abroad, local firms may be squeezed out, and wages may be low or the environment harmed.

00:00:53.750 --> 00:01:04.694
Step two: pick one clear gain. Step three: chain it to an outcome: sales, costs and profit for a firm; jobs, taxes and living standards for a country.

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:18.920
Here is a real question from Paper two in November 2021, about Huawei. Explain one benefit of being a multinational business. It is worth three marks, and no definition is needed.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:24.407
Mark one is the benefit. Selling in many countries spreads the business's risk.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:35.496
Mark two explains why. Huawei sells smartphones in many markets, so if demand falls in one country, perhaps in a recession, sales elsewhere make up for it.

00:01:36.050 --> 00:01:44.669
Mark three gives the consequence. Total revenue stays steadier, so the business is less likely to face cash problems or cut production.

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:54.120
Mistake one: answering for the wrong side. If the question asks about the host country, the firm's extra sales are not the answer.

00:01:54.700 --> 00:02:02.700
Mistake two: defining multinational when the question asks for a benefit. The definition earns nothing in an explain answer.

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:15.363
Now you try. A car maker opens a new factory in a country called Valoria, employing two thousand local people. Explain one benefit to Valoria. Pause and decide.

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:28.660
The factory creates two thousand new jobs. Those workers earn wages and gain new skills. They spend more in local shops, and the government collects more tax to spend on public services.

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:37.869
Remember the method: decide whose side, pick one clear gain, then chain it to an outcome. Now try the practice questions for this type.
